id":"part-0198","part":"43711.dat","color":0,"position":[177,-16,597],"matrix":[-0.707107,0,-0.707107,0,1,0,0.707107,0,-0.707107],"status":"step20 black 4x2 double-right wedge; placed tangent on outer semicircle r=250 around choir center x=0,z=420; later step44 ring supports the common center; module pitch matches 4-stud LDraw length; inferred from manual; endpoint and floor contacts provisional"},{"id":"part-0199","part":"43711.dat","color":0,"position":[113,-16,643],"matrix":[-0.891007,0,-0.45399,0,1,0,0.45399,0,-0.891007],"status":"step20 black 4x2 double-right wedge; placed tangent on outer semicircle r=250 around choir center x=0,z=420; later step44 ring supports the common center; module pitch matches 4-stud LDraw length; inferred from manual; endpoint and floor contacts provisional"},{"id":"part-0200","part":"43711.dat","color":0,"position":[39,-16,667],"matrix":[-0.987688,0,-0.156434,0,1,0,0.156434,0,-0.987688],"status":"step20 black 4x2 double-right wedge; placed tangent on outer semicircle r=250 around choir center x=0,z=420; later step44 ring supports the common center; module pitch matches 4-stud LDraw length; inferred from manual; endpoint and floor contacts provisional"},{"id":"part-0201","part":"87544.dat","color":19,"position":[249.199,-88,400.0],"matrix":[0.08,0,-0.996795,0,1,0,0.996795,0,0.08],"status":"step21 diagram-derived panel 1x2x3 Reinforced; two panels form a four-stud tangent segment on the r=250 LDU choir arc, centered at x≈249,z=420; bottom edge at floor y=-16 and upper studs at y=-88. Angular spacing, vertical origin and connection to step20 wedges remain provisional."},{"id":"part-0202","part":"87544.dat","color":19,"position":[249.199,-88,440.0],"matrix":[-0.08,0,-0.996795,0,1,0,0.996795,0,-0.08],"status":"step21 diagram-derived panel 1x2x3 Reinforced; two panels form a four-stud tangent segment on the r=250 LDU choir arc, centered at x≈249,z=420; bottom edge at floor y=-16 and upper studs at y=-88. Angular spacing, vertical origin and connection to step20 wedges remain provisional."}],"manual_observations":[{"pages":"16-17","steps":[13,14],"evidence":"Page 16 adds 2 short flat tiles, 7 long flat tiles, 2 small corner elements along three sides of the base perimeter. Page 17 begins a large grey floor panel with one olive 1x? marker tile and paired dark connector pieces; 12 floor tiles/plates are depicted.","placement":"The 12 LDraw 69729 tiles remain a 3x4 field. Their x extent [-80,40] LDU now meets the step18 4x6 mosaic right edge at x=-80; the later step44 choir semicircle is centered at x=0,z=420 beside this floor field. Contact of the arch with the tile field and exact z boundary remain provisional."},{"pages":"18-19","steps":[15,16],"evidence":"Step 15 adds two small tan plates, two tan longer plates, six dark 1x? plates and multiple grey plates to start paired interior footprints. Step 16 continues the floor with repeated dark/tan groups and a long grey edge strip; the 4x,3x,3x,2x and 4x,7x,1x quantities are shown.","placement":"The 24 paired 42862/48165 cells remain a 4x6 mosaic with bounds x=[-320,-80], z=[240,600] LDU. The step14 tile field begins at x=-80, providing an exact nominal edge match; later step44 places the choir arc center at x=0,z=420, 200 LDU east of the mosaic center. Internal color pattern and physical clutch remain provisional."},{"pages":"20-23","steps":[17,18,19,20],"evidence":"Step 17 shows four dark rectangular plates, one tan plate and four round tan studs. Step 18 adds 24 dark and 24 white triangular floor pieces. Step 19 adds 20 round tan studs. Step 20 adds repeated white/black wedge pieces in counts 5,5,8 and 5,5,10.","placement":"Later pages confirm a large repeated triangular nave floor and the axial/twin-bay alignment. They provide a backward constraint for steps 14-16, while leaving the current MPD origin and scale uncertain."},{"pages":"23","steps":[20],"evidence":"Instruction page 23 shows border detail groups with white counts 5/5/8 and black counts 5/5/10. The pieces differ in footprint across three silhouettes and surround the black/white triangular floor patch.","placement":"The 5-count silhouettes map to five complementary 42862/48165 pairs per color; the broad silhouettes map to 8 white 43710 and 10 black 43711 double wedges. The large wedges form two mirrored, concentric semicircular runs centered at x=0,z=420 (r=200 and 250 LDU); shifting the prior center +200 LDU places the choir arc beside the mosaic rather than through its center. The later step44 view shows 13 repeated three-stud top modules along the same choir arc: 13×60/π ≈248 LDU supports the outer radius 250. Exact endpoints, step14 floor contact, and clutch remain provisional."},{"pages":"37","steps":[44],"evidence":"Step 44 adds 13 repetitions each of a tan curved-top brick candidate and a tan 1x3 tile candidate along the outer choir arc. The assembled view shows an approximately semicircular repeated cap over the choir wall; 13 three-stud modules imply radius about 248 LDU.","placement":"Used as a backward geometric constraint for step20: it supports an outer radius near 250 LDU, while exact cap part identification, vertical level, wall connection coordinates, and physical clutch are not yet modeled/verified."},{"pages":"24","steps":[21],"evidence":"Step21 calls for two tall reinforced 1x2x3 panel elements plus separate top plates. The visible panel pair is four studs wide and sits on the curved choir-side floor edge. LDraw 87544 Panel 1x2x3 Reinforced matches the open side-support silhouette and 72-LDU height.","placement":"Two panels are placed side-by-side tangent to the r=250 choir semicircle, centered near its crown at x≈249,z=420. Their 40-LDU center pitch matches the 2-stud panel width. Vertical origin places the part bottom edge at floor y=-16 and top studs at y=-88. The exact step21 plate pieces, orientation, radial offset, and clutch remain provisional."}]}
